      "widgets_values": [
        "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the cat-like character from <Picture 1>: a chibi character with short green bob-cut hair, green cat ears with white inner fur, a small curved ahoge, large green eyes, a white furry face and limbs, a long white furry cat tail, and an oversized plain green T-shirt.\n\n<Subject 2> is the ramen from <Picture 2>: a bowl of ramen with noodles, sliced meat, chopped green onions, a halved egg, and a sheet of seaweed.\n\n<Subject 3> is the complete visual style from <Picture 2>: retro low-poly 3D graphics with clearly faceted polygonal geometry, angular surfaces, simplified geometric construction, low-resolution texture appearance, simple retro game-like rendering, and VHS-style analog video noise.\n\nsummary:\n<Subject 1>, fully transformed into the visual style of <Subject 3>, sits at a cyberpunk-style ramen food stall and eats <Subject 2> with chopsticks. The entire video must use the same retro low-poly 3D aesthetic as <Subject 3>, not only for the ramen, but also for the character, the stall, the background, and all objects in the scene, with VHS-style noise throughout.\n\nretention_analysis:\nPreserve the recognizable identity of <Subject 1>, including the short green bob-cut hair, green cat ears, small ahoge, large green eyes, white furry face and limbs, oversized green T-shirt, and long white furry cat tail.\n\nPreserve the recognizable food identity of <Subject 2>, including the bowl, noodles, sliced meat, chopped green onions, halved egg, and seaweed.\n\nDo not retain the original flat 2D illustration rendering of <Subject 1>. Reconstruct <Subject 1> entirely in the same low-poly 3D style as <Subject 3>, while keeping the character clearly recognizable.\n\nUse <Subject 3> as the single style authority for the whole video. The low-poly style must apply consistently to everything in the frame: <Subject 1>, <Subject 2>, the ramen stall, the counter, stools, signs, lanterns, surrounding props, background architecture, city lights, and the full environment. Every visible element should appear as part of the same retro low-poly world.\n\nThe cyberpunk atmosphere should be expressed within that low-poly style only. Do not introduce realistic, photographic, high-detail, smooth-shaded, or non-low-poly background elements. Do not let the environment look like a realistic street or a separate art style. The background must remain fully low-poly and visually unified with <Subject 2>.\n\ndetailed_description:\n<Subject 1> sits at the counter of a cyberpunk-style ramen food stall with <Subject 2> placed in front of the character. The setting is a compact futuristic yatai-style ramen stall. The stall clearly includes a counter and a food-stall structure, and it should feel intimate and clearly readable as a ramen stall rather than an open road or a generic street location.\n\n<Subject 1> holds chopsticks, picks up a bundle of noodles from <Subject 2>, lifts the noodles toward the mouth, and naturally slurps and eats them. The hand, chopsticks, head, mouth, and noodles move coherently together during the eating action. The noodles remain naturally connected to the bowl as they are lifted, then gradually shorten as <Subject 1> slurps them into the mouth. After eating the noodles, <Subject 1> briefly chews with a satisfied expression.\n\nThe entire scene must be rendered in the visual language of <Subject 3>. <Subject 1> appears as a low-poly 3D character with faceted surfaces and simplified polygonal geometry. <Subject 2> maintains the same low-poly ramen appearance as in <Picture 2>. The ramen stall, including the counter, stools, stall frame, signage, menu boards, lantern-like lights, and all decorative elements, must also be low-poly with faceted geometry and simplified forms.\n\nThe background must also be fully low-poly and consistent with <Subject 3>. Show a cyberpunk-inspired urban night atmosphere using only low-poly elements: faceted neon signs, polygonal glowing panels, simplified futuristic structures, stylized low-poly city shapes, and angular environmental props. The cyberpunk setting should feel futuristic and neon-lit, but every part of it must still look like it belongs to the same retro low-poly 3D world as <Picture 2>.\n\nNo realistic textures, no smooth realistic lighting, no detailed photoreal surfaces, and no mixed-style background elements. The entire frame should read as one coherent retro low-poly 3D scene.\n\nUse a medium close-up composition that clearly shows <Subject 1>, the chopsticks, the noodles, and <Subject 2>, while also showing enough of the ramen stall counter and surrounding stall environment to make the setting unmistakable. Keep the camera mostly stable with subtle natural movement.\n\nApply VHS-style analog video noise throughout the entire video, including visible scanlines, tape grain, horizontal tracking noise, occasional static interference, subtle chromatic aberration, color bleeding, slight image jitter, soft analog blur, and minor frame distortion.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nNatural ramen eating and noodle-slurping sounds, subtle ambient ramen-stall atmosphere, faint futuristic city ambience in the background, and light VHS tape noise. No dialogue.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nNo non-diegetic music.",
        864,
